# Caddy for local development and the single-node experiment.
#
# The admin API is the only thing configured here: the Node Agent programs every
# Platform Subdomain through it, so this file deliberately declares no site of its
# own. `local_certs` issues certificates from Caddy's internal CA, which is what
# makes `<ip>.nip.io` hostnames work over HTTPS without public DNS or an ACME
# account. On a real deployment with a public domain, replace it with an ACME
# issuer and the `ask` endpoint that only allows registered hostnames.
{
	admin 0.0.0.0:2019
	local_certs
	# The Node Agent writes routes into a server it creates itself, so the config
	# starts empty and stays empty until the first Deploy.
}
